<h2>Options After a Denial</h2>
<h3>Reconsideration with new evidence</h3>
<p>Many insurers will reconsider when presented with information the first adjuster did not have: a detailed estimate, close-up photos, moisture mapping, a contractor or engineer opinion, or weather data. A re-inspection with someone present to point out the damage can make a real difference in what gets seen.</p>
<h3>Splitting a partial denial</h3>
<p>When part of the loss is accepted, the accepted portion may still be underpaid. That part can be addressed through our <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid insurance claims</a> process while the denied portion is challenged separately.</p>
<h3>Appraisal for amount disputes</h3>
<p>If the dispute turns out to be about how much, not whether, <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">insurance appraisal</a> may be available under the policy.</p>
<h3>Legal advice</h3>
<p>Public adjusters are not attorneys and do not give legal advice. If a coverage denial seems wrong, the insurer alleges misrepresentation, or a deadline to sue may be near, consult a Texas attorney. Texas weather-related claim lawsuits require written pre-suit notice under Chapter 542A, and TWIA disputes have their own special rules.</p>

<h2>How a Port Arthur Public Adjuster Reviews a Denial</h2>
<p>When we review a denied claim, we read the letter against the policy, inspect the property ourselves and look for gaps between what the insurer documented and what is actually there. If the evidence supports it, we prepare documentation and a line-item estimate and present it to the insurer for reconsideration. If the denial appears correct under the policy, we will tell you that plainly. A Port Arthur Public Adjuster cannot promise a reversal, but a clear-eyed review helps you decide where to spend your time.</p>
<p>Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. Our article on <a href="/denied-insurance-claim-port-arthur/">what to do after a denied claim in Port Arthur</a> walks through the process in more depth, or you can request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>.</p>
